# Design Guidelines — Volt system

The site's look is inspired by landonorris.com: giant condensed display type, calm
green-tinted neutrals and one loud lime accent. Tokens live in `src/app/globals.css`.

## Color tokens

- `paper` (#f0f1e6): default page background
- `paper-2` (#e3e5d3): secondary background for cards and alternate sections
- `ink` (#15160f): text and the footer background
- `moss` (#262a1d): dark contrast blocks (selected work, off stack, outcomes, mobile menu)
- `volt` (#d4ff00): the single loud accent — never more than ~5% of a screen
- `volt-dim` (#aec72e): the accent on light backgrounds (numbers, arrows, dots), where pure volt lacks contrast
- `stone` (#b6b9a4): muted display type, such as the years in the career timeline

Rules:

1. Text is `ink` on paper and `paper` on moss/ink. Use opacity (`text-ink/85`, `text-paper/80`) for secondary text; keep it at `/70` or above for small text.
2. Volt is for emphasis: one primary button per view, underlines, hover fills, key numbers on moss.
3. Do not introduce new colors or gradients. No glassmorphism other than the sticky header.

## Typography

- Display: Anton via the `font-display` class. Always uppercase and tight (handled in CSS). Use it for headlines, numbers and names — never for body copy.
- Text: Mona Sans (`font-sans`, the default).
- Sizes are fluid with `clamp()`: page heroes `clamp(3.4rem,12vw,9.5rem)`, section headings `clamp(2.6rem,7vw,5.5rem)`.
- Eyebrows and labels: small, uppercase, wide tracking — use the `Eyebrow` component.
- No emojis in the interface.

## Layout

- Content width is `max-w-[1280px]` with `px-4`. Full-bleed color blocks wrap an inner container of that width.
- Sections breathe: `py-20 md:py-28`.
- Rows separated by hairlines (`border-t border-ink/15`) rather than boxed cards. Cards (`bg-paper-2 border border-ink/10 rounded-xl`) are for grids of peers, such as seasons and articles.
- Mobile first; the navigation collapses into the full-screen menu below `lg`.

## Shared components (`src/components/ui`)

- `PageHero`: eyebrow + display headline + lead, for every inner page
- `SectionHeading`: two-line display heading
- `Eyebrow`, `Chip`: labels and pills (both take `onDark` for moss blocks)
- `Reveal`: fade-and-rise on scroll; keeps pages as Server Components
- `CountUp`: animated numbers
- `ClosingCta`: the "Let's talk" closing block on every page except Contact

## Content and tone

- All copy lives in `src/content`, in English and Spanish. Never hardcode interface text in components.
- The site presents Lucas; it does not pitch services. Keep calls to action low-key ("Let's talk").
- Case studies describe projects generically (industry and region) and never name the client.
